      "message": "Fixed in patch set 5, by taking the fallback out rather than improving it: the\nexport now stops if `crypto.getRandomValues` is not there.\n\nThe fallback was never going to run -- `getRandomValues` is in every WKWebView\nand in Android\u0027s since long before the oldest version we build for, and it is\nnot one of the APIs a non-secure origin loses. So what it really was is a\nquieter way to fail: the one case it existed for is the case where the name\nstops being unguessable, and it would have gone on exporting without saying so.\n\nA test holds it: with `crypto` taken away, `attachmentScheme()` throws.",
