      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, and it is worse than a mask -- there is no failure it was there for.\nA picture this device does not hold is not an error: the daemon answers with an\nempty blob, which is what the missing-picture path already reads. So the only\nthing `onErrorReturnItem` could ever catch was something genuinely wrong, and\nit turned that into \"1 picture never arrived\" -- telling the reader their file\nis short of a picture when it is the export that broke.\n\nTaken out in patch set 5, on both clients (iOS had the same `catchAndReturn`).\nA failure now reaches the subscriber, which already says the export failed, and\na picture that never arrived still comes back empty, from the daemon.\n\nThe other half stands: the bytes are the document\u0027s own pictures, already held\nin the WebView, and an export that quietly stopped at a cap would be worse than\none that is large.",
